- Story & Context: Recorded inside an abandoned radio hut in Santos during a Category 2 storm, engineer Zé Silveira captured the moment lightning struck the local grid, burning out the master tape machine midway through a take. Teresa Prado continued playing her nylon-string bossa chords in pitch darkness while static bled through the broadcast monitors. The resulting track captures the literal death of the station's clock timer, blending ticking metronomes with huge, dubwise snare echoes. "The seconds stop turning the moment the tide comes in," whispers Teresa over the crumbling tape deck.
