Track 2: Desafinado para o Relógio de Areia
- Story & Context: Vocalist and radio operator Luiza Campos wrote this haunting track after waiting three hours at an empty train station for a lover who missed the final coastal express train. She hummed a flat, melancholic bossa melody directly into a CB radio microphone, which Zé routed through three cascading Space Echoes while giant synth pads mimicked blowing rain. The track captures her growing realization that the station schedule had been cancelled due to flash floods. "You left your watch upon my table, but the sands already drowned," she sings softly across the cavernous sub-bass weight.
